      "id": "tech-https://bbrouter.com/bbrouter/ben-eater-sap-1",
      "title": "Show HN: BBRouter – Ben Eater's 8-bit computer, simulated on 3D breadboards",
      "description": "Hi HN,I kept wiring Ben Eater's 8-bit computer wrong, so I built a realistic virtual breadboard editor.Some of the nice features are side-by-side diff, scope, schematics auto-sync, auto-router (BBRouter stands for breadboard router), and my favorites: upload from the real Arduino IDE and connect to your AI with MCP, let Claude & co build it or help you troubleshoot.The link is the SAP-1 running. You can orbit it, probe a hole with the scope, slow the clock down, play with the virtual displays for debugging, then you can actually build it following the step-by-step instructions.A side-goal is to create a community, there are quite a lot of simulators out there but mostly offline / too abstract to realistically use it for a real build. I also never found one that had a decent UI/UX and worked well on mobile or with a trackpad.Happy to answer anything, and tell me what breaks.p.s. Maker plan is $7/month; code HACKERNEWS makes the first month free and then $5/month for as long as you keep it.\n\nComments URL: https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=50321522\nPoints: 21\n# Comments: 6",
      "url": "https://bbrouter.com/bbrouter/ben-eater-sap-1",
